+          hardware switch functionalities through the switchdev API.
+
+          Switchdev is an API in the Linux kernel that allows hardware switches
+          to offload certain networking functions that would typically be
+          handled by the software (like bridging, VLANs, and routing).
+
+          Selecting this option will compile the driver as a module (if 'M' is
+          selected) or build it into the kernel (if 'Y' is selected). If unsure,
+          it is recommended to select 'M'.
